{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And Reuben answered them, etc.</b> One needs to know how a response can be justified on this matter; also, it says <b>saying</b> two times; also, it says <b>and also his blood, etc.</b>" "<b>Indeed,</b> the intent is that he came to respond to what they said — that the trouble came upon them because they did not have pity on their brother when he pleaded with them, etc. — and on this reasoning Reuben too would be included; therefore he answered and spoke, and this is the verse's saying <b>And Reuben answered them, saying</b> — for he should not be counted as guilty in this matter, for ״Did I not say to you, Do not sin against the child, etc.״ And even though he did not say so to them explicitly, but rather ״and do not lay a hand on him; cast him into [the pit]״ (Genesis 37:22), etc. — with all this, my intention was to say to you, Do not sin against the child. And this is the meaning of ״saying, Do not sin,״ as Scripture itself testified by saying ״to restore him to his father.״" "<b>And if</b> you say: On what basis did Reuben rely that his brothers would recognize his intention as having been so? On the contrary, in their view they showed greater mercy by selling him than by leaving him in the pit, as Scripture itself states (Genesis 37:27) that Judah said to them, ״Come, let us sell him, etc., and let our hand not be upon him״ — so what complaint is Reuben lodging by saying ״Did I not say to you, etc.״ — seeing that they acted according to his words and even added mercy as mentioned?" "Know that the core of Reuben's argument was in his saying ״and do not lay a hand on him,״ as I explained there — that he intended to save him from the hand of man, who has free choice and volition; this is the primary intent. And this argument is also valid to prevent them from selling him to strangers, whose deeds are acts of free will, and the sale also introduces him into the category of mortal danger from the strangers, and also because there exists the possibility of something evil. Go out and learn from what they said, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 86:3), that Potiphar bought him for male lie, and on this he was castrated. And this is the meaning of <b>Do not sin</b> — you — <b>against the child</b> — by doing anything to him; rather, cast him into the pit. And in any case: if he is liable to death, the wild beasts found there will kill him; and if not, it will be a sign of life — whereas this is not the case with the agency of a human hand. <b>And you did not listen</b> — meaning, you did not understand my words." "And as for what they said — that the trouble came because of the cruelty and because they did not accept his entreaty, while in the actual deed they committed no wrong — this is not so. Rather, <b>also his blood, behold, it is required</b> — for they are liable for sending hand against him, and they were placed in the danger of being accused as spies, which is a capital matter. And on this score as well, Reuben does not enter into the guilt with them, for he was not party to the sale. From this point on, Reuben was caught being with them alone, and upon completion of the investigation the guilty party will be held liable and the innocent one cleared in judgment. And also according to what I explained in connection with the verse ״but we are guilty״ — that their awakening was on account of the seizing of Shimon alone — the verse's meaning will also follow this path."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:48:13.155164340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}